["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Dataset/datasetSize", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note", "**NOTE:**\nThis property is deprecated and only included for backward compatibility.\nNew documents should use\n/Software/artifactSize\ninstead.\n\nHow large a dataset is.\n\nThe size is to be measured in bytes.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Software/packageUrl", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note", "A Package-URL (commonly pronounced and referred to as \"PURL\") is an attempt to standardize package representations\nin order to reliably identify and locate software packages.\nA packageUrl is a URL string which represents a package in a\nmostly universal and uniform way across programming languages, package\nmanagers, packaging conventions, tools, APIs and databases.\n\nA packageUrl is composed of seven components:\n\nscheme:type/namespace/name@version?qualifiers#subpath\n\n\nThe definition for each component can be found in the corresponding\nAnnex of this document.\nKnown type definitions can be found in the\nPackage-URL type definitions <https://github.com/package-url/purl-spec/blob/main/types/README.md>.\n\nComponents are designed such that they form a hierarchy from the most\nsignificant on the left to the least significant components on the right.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Software/packageUrl", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Software/", "globalId", "", ""]
